,A,A,A,A,A)
--- expect
text "2"
===

% --- Evaluate, then coerce (SPEC 6.2). The answer is the plain tree's: every operand is
% evaluated left to right, and only then coerced and checked.

### name: ord.operands.binary-left-notnum-right-div-zero
--- note
Evaluate, then coerce (SPEC 6.2): the right operand is evaluated before the left is coerced, so the division by zero, not "abc", is the error.
--- source
"abc" + 1/0
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:10
===

### name: ord.operands.binary-left-notnum-right-undef
--- note
Evaluate, then coerce: B is undefined, and that is found before A = "x" is coerced.
--- source
A = "x"; A + B
--- expect
error E_UNDEF_VAR at 1:14
===

### name: ord.operands.binary-left-notnum-right-undef-unplanned
--- note
The same program with the right operand wrapped so no host plans it: every host already agreed.
--- source
A = "x"; A + (C = B)
--- expect
error E_UNDEF_VAR at 1:19
===

### name: ord.operands.binary-left-notnum-right-undef-if
--- note
Same, through IF (unplannable).
--- source
A = "x"; A + IF(TRUE, B, 1)
--- expect
error E_UNDEF_VAR at 1:23
===

### name: ord.operands.comparison-left-text-right-undef
--- note
Comparisons were never planned and already evaluated both first.
--- source
A = "x"; A < B
--- expect
error E_UNDEF_VAR at 1:14
===

### name: ord.operands.null-minus-missing-coalesced
--- note
NULL - MISSING: MISSING is undefined, which ?? catches (E_UNDEF_VAR), so the result is 7. A plan coerced NULL first and raised E_NULL, which ?? does not catch.
--- source
(NULL - MISSING) ?? 7
--- expect
text "7"
===

### name: ord.operands.null-equals-missing-coalesced
--- note
The comparison twin of the above: 7.
--- source
(NULL == MISSING) ?? 7
--- expect
text "7"
===

### name: ord.operands.compound-assign-rhs-error
--- note
A compound assignment evaluates its right side, then coerces both.
--- source
A = "x"; A += (1/0)
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:17
===

### name: ord.operands.text-times-div-zero
--- note
Multiplication twin of binary-left-notnum-right-div-zero.
--- source
x = "abc"; x * (1/0)
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:18
===

### name: ord.operands.index-expression-error
--- note
An error inside an index expression.
--- source
X = "x"; A = 1; A[X + (1/0)] = 1
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:25
===

### name: ord.operands.assignment-rhs-error
--- note
The assignment target is not the issue: the right-hand side evaluates X + (1/0) with evaluate-then-coerce.
--- source
X = "x"; A = X + (1/0)
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:20
===

### name: ord.operands.record-fields-text-plus-missing
--- note
Data-shaped: X["a"] is text, X["b"] is a missing key (E_NO_KEY, which is found first).
--- source
X = RECORD("a","q"); X["a"] + X["b"]
--- expect
error E_NO_KEY at 1:32
===

### name: ord.operands.record-fields-compare
--- note
Comparison twin.
--- source
X = RECORD("a","q"); X["a"] > X["b"]
--- expect
error E_NO_KEY at 1:32
===

### name: ord.operands.shallow-dead-branch-pair
--- note
The shallow half of the dead-branch pair: the same live program as deep-dead-branch-pair.
--- source
A = "x"; IF(TRUE, A + (1/0), 1)
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:25
===

### name: ord.operands.deep-dead-branch-pair
--- note
The same live program beside a 260-term dead branch of the IF. Whether a math plan applies must not change the answer or its position.
--- source
A = "x"; IF(TRUE, A + (1/0), )
--- expect
error E_DIV_ZERO at 1:25
===

### name: ord.operands.data-shaped-map
--- note
Data-shaped: r["a"] / r["b"] over a row lacking b: E_NO_KEY, not E_NOT_NUM.
--- source
L = LIST(RECORD("a","q","c","y")); MAP(L, r, r["a"] / r["b"])
--- expect
error E_NO_KEY at 1:56
===

% --- Entering an aggregate body costs no extra evaluation level (SPEC 6.4): the body is
% an ordinary expression one level below the call. Each shape is pinned on both sides
% of its boundary. JS, C++ and Lisp charged one level for the binder scope and raised
% a term early. A fused FILTER-in-FILTER costs what the unfused pair costs (6.2).

### name: lim.eval-depth.aggregate-body-filter-just-under
--- note
198 AND terms in the outer predicate of a FILTER: still runs.
--- setup
